## Context

Apply the 0716 contract to the Indonesian JETP from the 2022 declaration to the
collection date. Cover the CIPP and its updates, the secretariat/JETP Delivery
Unit, PLN, the official pipeline, the 54 projects reported in 2025, the donors
and the fate of the coal retirements.

## Test

The coverage check fails as long as the matrix has no verdict for
JETP Indonesia/JETP Delivery Unit, MEMR, PLN, IPG, GFANZ and each named public
donor. Project totals may not add up need, announcement, MoU, approval,
signature and disbursement.

## Exit criteria

- [x] CIPP 2023 and later updates collected or absence proven
- [x] The pipeline projects are identified and sourced individually
- [x] The 54 projects/USD 1.1 bn announced in March 2025 are reconciled with the later snapshot of 53 projects at 30 November 2025
- [x] Coal retirements and ETM financing have a distinct physical status
- [x] Indonesia coverage check passes

## Result

The matrix contains 74 Indonesian projects, all with a terminal verdict:
66 `collected`, 6 `central_only` and 2 `blocked`. The 44 grant programmes and
the 9 approved loan or equity projects were reviewed. The 19 financial-pipeline
projects, the AICET programme and the 14 CMEA tracking entries are linked to
sources and to explicit dry searches. The 2023 CIPP contains 437 plan lines and
annex 1 of 2025 contains 1,142.

The March 2025 milestone (54 projects, USD 1.1 bn) and that of 30 November 2025
(53 projects) remain two distinct dated observations. Financial and physical
states are not merged: notably, Cirebon remains without evidence of retirement,
while the later announcements for SEG, Sutami and Legok are recorded as
separate physical events.
